Created the Plone Aurora add-on. It puts a button for each identity provider on Aurora's login page, starts a sign-in at `/login-identity/start/<provider>`, and finishes it at `/login-identity` -- the same callback path the Volto add-on uses -- storing the session in Aurora's own cookie. A magic link arriving at the callback signs in the same way. The backend is called through a virtual-host URL naming Aurora's public address, so the provider sends the user back to Aurora, and the backend's flow cookie is passed through to the browser and back. Translations come from `identity-core`'s catalogues, regenerated with `pnpm i18n`. @sneridagh
